From 6adde23e71e6abaec6f2b32784985ccb5ccdd686 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:26:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Field operations: two-dimensional kernels, dense copies, SYCL
 queue

- the kernels of the five backends process the points and the components
  along two dimensions instead of computing a 64 bits division and
  remainder per value; consecutive threads still process consecutive
  points of a component.
- Kokkos: dense copies and fills by Kokkos::deep_copy; OpenMP: dense
  copies by omp_target_memcpy.
- CUDA and HIP: the size of the grid is checked; the memset of a fill by
  a positive zero assumes real values of 8 bytes, checked statically.
- SYCLFieldOperations copies the queue, a handle, instead of keeping a
  reference.
---
